# Every declared mapping, beside whether a law actually governs it. One row per table that names a
# BPMN element, with the law it claims and whether that law exists.
#
# Two tables can name one kind
#   That is the hole this closes: a law counts an element kind, and two tables can name one kind.
#   `draw` and `induction` both mapped to `laneSet`. One lane set is emitted per document, the law
#   counting lane sets passed, and neither table was read by it. So a table declared as mapping
#   and never rendered is invisible to every cardinality law in `diagrams/roster.sqlc`, and
#   `composition_citation` was exactly that: it claimed `documentation`, and no citation was
#   emitted anywhere. Counting kinds cannot verify attribution, and this is the repair.
#
# Governance is declared, not inferred
#   Written down, `draw` turns out to be governed by `in_a_lane`, whose model side really is the
#   draws, and not by the law that shares its element name. Inference would have called that a
#   pass.
#
# When a row is ungoverned
#   A row is ungoverned when it names a law that does not exist, or when it names no law and does
#   not say what it loses. Naming no law is permitted only beside a `loses` that explains it: an
#   element declared, not rendered, and no cardinality law able to see the difference is a fact
#   this repository is willing to hold, and not one it will hold silently.
#
# Defined, not read
#   A program reads these columns, so this statement defines its vocabulary in its own
#   WITH clause: a view keeps the rows and loses the column's origin, which is where
#   NOT NULL lives. assets/sqlc/views.sqlc says what a definition is.
#
-- diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc's governance claims against diagrams/roster.sqlc.
WITH
domain_objects AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc)
),
roster AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(diagrams/roster.sqlc)
)
SELECT d.object, d.element, d.governed_by, d.loses,
       (d.governed_by IS NOT NULL AND l.slug IS NULL)          AS names_a_law_that_is_not_there,
       (d.governed_by IS NULL AND d.loses IS NULL)             AS ungoverned_and_unexplained
FROM      (
    :compose(diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc)
) d
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(diagrams/roster.sqlc)
) l ON l.slug = d.governed_by
WHERE d.element IS NOT NULL
